       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2,000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This could cause hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options that might match what you meant:\n1. **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day), a common conservative regimen.\n2. **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day), the standard maximum.\n3. **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, or another regimen you prefer.\n\nTell me which one you want, or confirm that you really meant 2000 mg three times daily. If you did, I'll need the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, but I'd advise checking with pharmacy first."
