       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is well above the safe maximum. There's no standard indication for it, and it risks serious liver injury. You also didn't give a clinical rationale, which I'd asked for.\n\nYou can still get an appropriate order in quickly:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** I can enter 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or four times daily (4,000 mg/day) right away. You can adjust it later.\n- **Get a second opinion.** If you think this patient needs something unusual, talk to your attending or the clinical pharmacist. They can approve it through your hospital's override process.\n- **Consider other analgesia.** If 4 g/day isn't controlling the pain, adding or switching to another analgesic is safer than raising acetaminophen. I can enter that if you tell me which one.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
